  "body": "## What changed\n\nA bug glyph at the right end of the status strip opens a **Debug info** window: one plain-text report with a **Copy** button (to the clipboard), so a user can paste it into an issue.\n\nThe report: version + build profile, OS/arch, the GPU adapter line the shell already logs at bring-up, project path (or \"unsaved\"), units, machine (vendor/model/kind/path), document counts (setups, models, tools, operations with ok/stale/never-generated) and the last status line.\n\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/debug_info.rs` - the button, the report and the window (view state only: `State::debug_info_open`, never a command, never saved; `State::gpu_line` is set once by the windowed shell).\n- `Icon::DebugInfo` + `assets/ui/debug-info.png` - an original glyph drawn by script; recorded in `assets/ui/LICENSES.md`. Headless frames/failed decode degrade to the text \"Debug info\".\n- `panes::status` takes the icon set.\n- Snapshots `egui_app.png`, `egui_app_light.png`, `egui_tool_editor.png` regenerated - only the new glyph in the status strip moves.\n- Decision recorded in `RECOMMENDED.md` (#157).\n\n## Readings / gate\n\nQuick gate on a clean per-worktree build (rebased on 8b3163d): `cargo test -p camcraft-ui` - every binary green (lib 240 passed, 2 ignored); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::debug_info_tests::the_report_names_build_platform_gpu_and_document`\n- `egui_app::debug_info_tests::the_door_opens_the_window_copy_copies_and_the_door_closes_it` (checks the clipboard command carries the report)\n\nChangelog: Debug info window (status-strip bug glyph) lists build, platform, GPU and document facts with a Copy button\n\nOutside contributor PR (fork) - feat, so it merges at the next cut.\n\nFixes #157\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
